            <ArticleTitle>Radioactive tracers and the heart.</ArticleTitle>
            <Pagination>
                <MedlinePgn>83-98</MedlinePgn>
            </Pagination>
            <Abstract>
                <AbstractText>The most widely used tracer for the study of the heart muscle is thallium-201. The principal advantage of radioactive tracers in the study of the heart is that they tell us about regional as well as a overall function. In some cases a regional abnormality may be detected before the overall function of the heart is impaired.</AbstractText>
            </Abstract>
